+## Try-on (`/try-on`, built on branch `tryon-portal`, not live)
+
+A shopper adds one photo and sees one of 20 pieces on herself: a photoreal
+"AI preview" from Nano Banana Pro through the Lovable AI gateway, with the
+real listing photo and the millimetre size beside it, then adds the exact
+variant shown. Unlisted and noindex: `/try-on` (hub), `/try-on/<handle>`
+(studio), `/tryon` (alias, query kept). Never in `scripts/routes.ts` (the
+prerenderer refuses noindex pages). The spec is the judge's design of 30 Oct
+2026 (scratchpad `portal-oct30/spec/SPEC.md`).
+
+Where it lives: `supabase/functions/tryon/` (the edge function: every prompt,
+the 20 references, quota, the gateway calls), `supabase/migrations/
+20261101000000_tryon.sql`, `src/lib/tryon/` (photo prep, session store,
+client, copy, analytics), `src/components/tryon/` and `src/pages/TryOn.tsx`
+(the screens), `src/data/tryOnPieces.ts` (browser manifest) and
+`src/data/tryOnHandles.ts` (the only try-on file the product page may import).
+
+Two flags keep a publish inert, and both must be flipped on purpose:
+- `TRYON_ENABLED` (function secret): anything but `on` answers 503 "resting".
+- `TRY_ON_ENTRY_LIVE` (`src/data/tryOnHandles.ts`): the product page's "Try on"
+  chip under the heart. False through the pilot; `TryOnEntry` renders nothing.
+
+Function secrets: `LOVABLE_API_KEY` (exists only once Lovable AI is enabled),
+`TRYON_SALT` (32+ random characters, else 503), `TRYON_DEVICE_DAILY` (5),
+`TRYON_IP_DAILY` (30, loose for carrier NAT), `TRYON_DAILY_CAP` (100),
+`TRYON_VERIFY` (strict | log | off), `TRYON_RENDER_ID` (allow-list only),
+`TRYON_EXTRA_ORIGINS` (a preview origin, never in production),
+`TRYON_ALLOW_UNCERTIFIED` (serve-local only), `TRYON_GATEWAY_URL` (loopback
+only, tests), optional `TURNSTILE_SECRET`. Until Lovable applies the migration
+the function fails closed (503, not_configured).
+
+Rules that are the point, not details:
+- The model is pinned in `gateway.ts`: `google/gemini-3-pro-image` (Nano Banana
+  Pro; the `-preview` id is the only alternative), checks on
+  `google/gemini-3.8-flash`. Every prompt is built server-side from
+  `pieces.ts`; the browser sends only enums. `npx vite-node
+  scripts/tryon/print-prompts.ts` prints them byte for byte.
+- A piece is offered only once the owner has certified it. To certify: render
+  it with the printed prompts on synthetic subjects (never a real person's
+  photo), the owner approves, then set `certified: 'YYYY-MM-DD'` in BOTH
+  `src/data/tryOnPieces.ts` and `supabase/functions/tryon/pieces.ts` and add
+  the handle to `TRY_ON_LIVE_HANDLES` (tests keep all three equal). Approved
+  demo renders go in `public/tryon/demo/` with `demo: true`. Off the real shop
+  (`window.__nairaProd` false) uncertified pieces show, labelled, for testing.
+- The photo is never stored: not in Storage, the database, logs or browser
+  storage. It is re-encoded on the phone (EXIF and GPS gone), shown only as a
+  `blob:` URL (never `data:`), inside `data-clarity-mask` containers, and every
+  URL is revoked on Delete photo, pagehide and 30 minutes idle. Browser storage
+  holds only `naira_tryon_device` (a random uuid, never `naira_vid`),
+  `naira_tryon` (handles tried, also the order's cart attribute),
+  `naira_tryon_consent` and `naira_tryon_tips`.
+- Nothing goes to Meta: no new pixel or CAPI event. AddToCart still fires only
+  from CartContext. Clarity gets allow-listed event names only
+  (`src/lib/tryon/analytics.ts`).
+- Add opens the bag at the tap; the line comes from `src/lib/oneTapLine.ts`,
+  shared with the product page's "Complete the look", so the two never
+  disagree. Nothing is added from first-paint data.
+- The result screen's code is fetched during the wait; its chunk is in
+  `optionalChunk.ts` so a failed fetch never triggers the stale-build reload
+  (which would lose the photo and a paid preview).
+
+Owner launch blockers (cannot be done from a session): enable Lovable AI;
+turn OFF "AI app context" (on by default, keeps full requests, the selfie
+included, for 90 days); ask Lovable how long request images are kept; set a
+Lovable AI usage limit with blocking; have Lovable apply the migration;
+publish the privacy section (`/privacy#try-on`) before `TRYON_ENABLED=on`;
+certify each piece. Then a smoke in the Lovable preview with
+`TRYON_EXTRA_ORIGINS` set to the preview origin, one real render per
+category. Run `npx vite-node scripts/tryon/check-refs.ts` before every
+publish (every reference must answer 200 image).
+
 ## Conventions
 
 - Comments explain *why*, never *what*. Match the density already in the file.
